laurel mu late/0101: LATE memory layout, used instead of mu 0101 with `MU_RAM_LAYOUT=late scripts/laurel/mu-build.sh` (applied after
every other mu patch). For the case that the static map of 0101 kills Mu (UEFI then allocates above 4 GiB from its first DXE; a
Qualcomm binary with 32-bit DMA could fail). "Pool RAM Guard" 0x80000000 + 16 MiB and "Pool RAM" 0x90000000 + 0x51000000 (to
0xE1000000: GPU pool 0xC0000000 + 512 MiB, modem pool 0xE0000000 + 16 MiB) reserved; "UEFI RAM" 0x81000000 + 240 MiB conventional,
the highest RAM until RamManagerDxe runs, so every early allocation stays below 4 GiB. No static "Kernel RAM": RamManagerDxe maps
the bank C hole 0xE1000000-0x1C0000000 late (one run; the DarwinBoot window 0xE1004000 + 3264 MiB, as with 0101). NegroniBootMemoryDxe
gets NEGRONIMEM_ADD_BELOW 0xE1000000 from the dsc (the define is a no-op elsewhere), or it would add 0xE1000000-0x100000000 as an
early DT hole and UEFI's early allocations would cut the window run. Any RAM size (bank C from SMEM, not hard-coded).
mkadt.py --dram auto recognises this FD by its "UEFI RAM" entry and plans the same window.
diff --git a/Platforms/OnePlus/negroniPkg/Drivers/NegroniBootMemoryDxe/NegroniBootMemoryDxe.c b/Platforms/OnePlus/negroniPkg/Drivers/NegroniBootMemoryDxe/NegroniBootMemoryDxe.c
